;; Slots a scrutinee leaves dead (HE4d; review of HE4d's runs: a list consumed by length was kept whole by a case
;; frame's slot). A case frame keeps its activation's slots, all of them, while GHC's keeps only the live variables:
;; a slot nothing after a call reads (the alternatives of the cases pending in the same activation) would keep what it
;; holds alive for the whole call. So a call or an entry inside a case's scrutinee clears, once it has read its
;; arguments, every slot its activation's code reads that no pending continuation reads (App.kill, Enter.kill; in tail
;; position scope.atail's clr does it). A thunk's free variables are never cleared (a reverted thunk needs them).

